Question 1: What are all the parent disease categories that Gaucher Disease belongs to, ordered from closest to broadest?
MATCH (d:ref_disease {disease_name: 'Gaucher Disease'})-[:IS_A*1..10]->(ancestor:ref_disease)
RETURN 
  ancestor.disease_name,
  ancestor.description,
  length(shortestPath((d)-[:IS_A*]-(ancestor))) AS distance
ORDER BY distance

Question 2: Which existing FDA-approved drugs can be repurposed to target Gaucher Disease?
MATCH (d:ref_disease {disease_name: 'Gaucher Disease'})<-[:mapDisease]-(tdm:target_disease_map)-[:mapTarget]->(bt:biologicaltarget)
WITH d, bt
MATCH (bt)<-[:mapInteractionTarget]-(sti:substancetargetinteraction)-[:mapInteractionSubstance]->(s:substance)
WHERE s.approval_status = 'FDA Approved' 
  AND NOT EXISTS {
    MATCH (s)<-[:mapInteractionSubstance]-(sim:substance_indication_map)-[:mapDisease]->(dd:ref_disease)
    WHERE dd.disease_name = 'Gaucher Disease'
  }
RETURN DISTINCT 
  s.substancename AS RepurposedCandidate, 
  bt.targetname AS BiologicalTarget, 
  sti.isprimarymechanism AS IsPrimaryMechanism

Question 3: Find me any approved drugs that could treat diseases related to lysosomal storage issues.
MATCH (d:ref_disease)-[:IS_A*1..10]->(parent:ref_disease)
WHERE parent.disease_name = 'Lysosomal Storage Disease'
   OR parent.description = 'Lysosomal Storage Diseases'
MATCH (d)<-[:mapDisease]-(tdm:target_disease_map)-[:mapTarget]->(bt:biologicaltarget)
MATCH (bt)<-[:mapInteractionTarget]-(sti:substancetargetinteraction)-[:mapInteractionSubstance]->(s:substance)
WHERE s.approval_status = 'FDA Approved'
RETURN DISTINCT 
  d.disease_name AS SpecificDisease, 
  bt.targetname AS BiologicalTarget, 
  s.substancename AS PotentialTreatment, 
  sti.isprimarymechanism AS IsPrimaryMechanism

Question 4: Which vendors currently hold active contracts with multiple jurisdiction indicators, and do they have any outstanding invoices past their due date?
MATCH (po:PurchaseOrder)-[:HAS_CONTRACT]->(c:Contract), 
      (po)-[:HAS_VENDOR]->(v:Vendor)
WHERE c.multiplejurisdictionindicator IS NOT NULL 
  AND c.multiplejurisdictionindicator <> ''
WITH v, collect(DISTINCT c.contractid) AS contractIds
MATCH (v)<-[:HAS_VENDOR]-(inv:Invoice)
WHERE date(inv.duedate) < date() 
  AND (inv.status IS NULL OR inv.status <> 'Paid')
WITH v, 
     contractIds, 
     collect(DISTINCT inv.invoiceid) AS overdueInvoiceIds, 
     COUNT(inv) AS overdueCount
WHERE overdueCount > 0
RETURN 
  v.vendorid AS vendorId, 
  v.vendorname AS vendorName, 
  contractIds, 
  overdueInvoiceIds, 
  overdueCount

Question 5: Which invoices are tied to aging report data with over 60 days past due specifically because of an applied hold reason?
MATCH (a:AgingReportData)-[:HAS_INVOICE]->(i:Invoice)<-[:HAS_INVOICE]-(h:HoldReason)
WHERE a.dayspastdue > 60
RETURN 
  i.invoiceid AS invoiceId, 
  i.invoicenumber AS invoiceNumber, 
  a.dayspastdue AS daysPastDue, 
  h.reason AS holdReason, 
  h.holddate AS holdDate

Question 6: For projects past their planned end date, what is the variance between the budgeted amount and the total invoice product amount billed?
MATCH (p:Project)
WHERE date(p.plannedenddate) < date()
OPTIONAL MATCH (i:Invoice)-[:HAS_PROJECT]->(p)
WITH p, coalesce(sum(i.totalinvoiceproductamount), 0) AS billedAmount
RETURN 
  p.projectid AS projectId, 
  p.budgetedamount AS budgetedAmount, 
  billedAmount, 
  p.budgetedamount - billedAmount AS variance
ORDER BY variance DESC

Question 7: Which approval hierarchies contain steps where the required approval limit exceeds the maximum approval amount of the assigned approval process?
MATCH (h:ApprovalHierarrchy)-[:HAS_APPROVAL_ROLE]->(r:ApprovalRole), 
      (h)-[:HAS_APPROVAL_PROCESS]->(p:ApprovalProcess)
WHERE r.approvallimit > p.maximumapprovalamount
RETURN DISTINCT 
  h.approvalhierarchyid AS hierarchyId, 
  h.approvallevel AS hierarchyLevel, 
  r.role AS roleName, 
  r.approvallimit AS requiredApprovalLimit, 
  p.approvalprocessid AS processId, 
  p.maximumapprovalamount AS maxApprovalAmount

Question 8: Show me contracts with an automatic renewal indicator where the vendor has a negative compliance status, and list the associated penalty amounts.
MATCH (c:Contract)-[:HAS_CONTRACT_TERM]->(ct:ContractTerm), 
      (c)-[:IS_CONTRACT_OF]->(po:PurchaseOrder)-[:HAS_VENDOR]->(v:Vendor)
WHERE c.automaticrenewalindicator IS NOT NULL 
  AND c.automaticrenewalindicator <> '' 
  AND v.compliancestatus = 'Negative'
RETURN 
  c.contractid AS contractId, 
  c.automaticrenewalindicator AS autoRenewalIndicator, 
  v.vendorid AS vendorId, 
  collect(ct.penaltyamount) AS penaltyAmounts
